  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — skewness — is not explicitly considered or discussed in the verbal report. The individual focuses on the probability of winning a high sum (25% vs 20%) and evaluates whether the risk of a higher payout in B is worth it. This reflects a concern with probability of success, not with the distributional shape (skewness). The decision reason requires evaluating whether one lottery has a greater concentration of probability on favorable outcomes (i.e., more left-skewed), which would imply a higher probability of the positive outcome relative to the zero outcome. While A has a slightly higher probability of a positive outcome (25% vs 20%), the report does not frame this in terms of skewness. The justification does not invoke or reference the concept of skewness or left-skewness. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason involving skewness. The reasoning is different and based on probability of winning rather than distributional asymmetry.",
